  message: "THE FILED CENSUS WAS WRONG ABOUT TWO OF THE FOUR LANGUAGES (LIVE.md rule 2:\nright that something is thin, wrong about which part). Counted 2026-09-03 by\nfile extension under ~/ALL_REPOS/*/<repo>:\n  kotlin  detekt        1,106 .kt     whole_bunch_of_repos/detekt   (CLI, file I/O)\n  objc    AFNetworking     49 .m      whole_bunch_of_repos/AFNetworking (network)\n  swift   VernissageServer 906, Alamofire 96 (whole_bunch_of_repos)\n  scala   docspell 872, http4s 652 (whole_bunch_of_repos)\nSo swift and scala already have TWO repos each and need nothing; kotlin and\nobjc have ONE each. The filing's \"0 repos\" for kotlin/objc did not look in\nwhole_bunch_of_repos, or its language heuristic missed them -- the instrument\nwas not kept, so which is not recoverable. Cloning the second of each now via\n~/clone_all.py into whole_bunch_of_repos: square/okhttp (kotlin, network I/O)\nand SDWebImage/SDWebImage (objc, network + disk cache). Paths will be recorded\nin ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/sovup_corpus_09032026/repos.txt when the clones\nland; 1-repo mini trial before any experiment, per the experiment-design\nplaybook."  # 5734
