  message: "DONE 2026-09-03. Two repos per language are on disk and recorded in\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/sovup_corpus_09032026/repos.txt (name language path):\n  kotlin  detekt (1,106 .kt, already present) + okhttp (573 .kt, cloned; network I/O)\n  objc    AFNetworking (49 .m, already present) + SDWebImage (104 .m, cloned; network + disk cache)\n  swift   VernissageServer (906) + Alamofire (96, already present)\n  scala   docspell (872) + http4s (652, already present)\nClones via ~/clone_all.py into whole_bunch_of_repos (github.com allowlisted;\nclone.log: total=2 success=2). 1-REPO MINI TRIAL run as the experiment-design\nplaybook requires: okhttp, `io-boundaries --format json --minimal`, cold\ncache, 58 s wall / 340 MB RSS -- so a two-repo kotlin arm is minutes, not\nhours. Its result is not a measurement but it IS WI-nasuf's kotlin cell on a\nreal repo: 49 kotlin chains, all `kotlin.io.ConsoleKt.println`/`print`\n(function-kind), ZERO method-kind chains despite okhttp's Socket / Buffer /\nFile surface. README in the lab dir.\nWhat this does NOT settle: the four repos I found already present were not\nseen by the filing's census, and that instrument was not kept, so whether it\nlooked in the wrong directory or misjudged the language is not recoverable.\nCount by file extension under ~/ALL_REPOS/*/<repo> before filing a corpus gap."  # d61a
